invariant: INV-16
file: src/mldsa.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh keccak
reason: the verifier samples each entry of A through the call that takes
  no value, so a verification under CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3 runs the 56
  SHAKE128 streams of ExpandA on sha3.c. Every verdict stays right, so no
  vector notices. bin/mldsa_runtime_test counts each SHAKE call on each
  path under every ch_cfg.cpu value, for mldsa87_verify_cpu and for the
  check after each signature. Only an arm64 object that clang compiled has
  the instructions' path, so the script builds the binary with clang for
  arm64 and runs it under qemu-aarch64.

--- old
        if (!mld_sample_ntt_cpu(cpu, entry, pk, (uint8_t)j, (uint8_t)i)) {
--- new
        if (!mld_sample_ntt(entry, pk, (uint8_t)j, (uint8_t)i)) {
